  1469                              <1> ; detect_disks -- IDENTIFY C: and D: (unless done, or found absent) with
  1470                              <1> ; a timeout of CX units (15 ms): show the model name (and the LBA size if
  1471                              <1> ; it is larger than what CHS reaches) and, if "Auto-Detect Disks at Boot"
  1472                              <1> ; is on, set the drive up as type 47 with the geometry the drive reports.
  1473                              <1> ; A drive is only asked if CMOS has it or auto-detection is on.
