  1676                              <1> ; ---------------------------------------------------------------------
  1677                              <1> ; measure_clock -> [ST_MHZ] (MHz x 10): a timing loop of 32 DIVs per
  1678                              <1> ; pass is built in RAM (0:7C00) and timed by PIT channel 2. The setup
  1679                              <1> ; uses 8 DIVs per pass; the longer pass makes the reading much less
  1680                              <1> ; sensitive to slow code fetches while the cache is still off (early in
  1681                              <1> ; POST). A reading not within 1/16 of a standard clock is not shown.
  1682                              <1> ; ---------------------------------------------------------------------
  1683                              <1> measure_clock:
  1684 00000442 06                  <1>     push es
  1685 00000443 68C007              <1>     push TLOOP_SEG
